    dst->content.encoded.typeId = *typeId;
    return ByteString_decodeBinary(&dst->content.encoded.body);
}
```

If `ByteString_decodeBinary` fails, `dst->content.encoded.body.data` is set to NULL by `Array_decodeBinary`. But `dst->content.encoded.typeId` was already set. So `ExtensionObject_deleteMembers` would free `typeId` and `body` - both should be safe since body.data is NULL.

Let me think about the actual double-free scenario. The crash is in `ExtensionObject_deleteMembers` called from `UA_Array_delete` called from `Array_decodeBinary`. So we have an array of ExtensionObjects where one fails to decode.

